																		&quot;When We Didn&#039;t Dream&quot; - An SCP Tale Seeking Greenlight
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gravyismad" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4854120); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4854120&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609574990" alt="gravyismad" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4854120)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gravyismad" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4854120); return false;" >gravyismad</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608149507 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Dec 2020 20:11</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846470">
									

<p>A troublesome teenager utilizes mysterious livestock to control his dreams. A tale about SCP-1498.</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight:</strong> <em>Recieved</em></p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p>This tale doesn't take place in The Foundation itself. It's based around one specific SCP before it was contained.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A teenager by the name of Ty encounters SCP-1498 in the woods, and begins to abuse its abilities. However, when he slowly starts to become an instance of SCP-1498, he struggles to find help. This takes place a month before SCP-1498's original containment date.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Taking place in august of 1965, just before SCP-1498 (which this tale is about) is contained, a troublesome teenager, Ty, stumbles across SCP-1498 in the woods and learns that he can order dreams from the SCP. He begins to abuse the ability, spending most of his time asleep, dreaming. However, when his body begins to slowly turn into instances of the SCP, he attempts to find &quot;The Oneiroi Collective&quot; (the people who possibly designed the SCP) to help him. However, upon searching phone books, he discovers that the phone number to call them only exists on the instances of SCP-1498. He hurries back to where he last saw them, but they've vanished completely. Luckily, a phone wire that goes through the woods leads him to an abandoned office building, where he finds the livestock entering. Ty catches up to them, managing to get on the phone with The Oneiroi Collective. However, it's too late, and Ty completely transforms into an instance of SCP-1498-1, mindlessly wandering back into the woods, ironically dreaming of the days when he didn't dream at all.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> The realization that Ty basically has no way out of the situation he's in. This is the foundation of most of the tension throughout the tale, as it will seem almost completely hopeless. Which, by the end, it's revealed that it was, indeed, hopeless. At least, that's the goal I'll try to achieve with this tale.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Obviously, this is a rough outline of what happens, and it will almost certainly change (hopefully for the better) as critiques come in. I'm also not the author of SCP-1498, and as so tried to keep this story as distant from the lore set up in the SCP itself.</p>
<p>Here's a link to SCP-1498, which this tale is based on: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1498">http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1498</a><br />
<em>P.S, thanks for the tip Zyn, I'll take note of that</em></p>

