														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4856022">
									

<p>Hey! How are you doing?</p>
<p>Thank you so much for the response.</p>
<p>The ending is bleak, and I definitely think it could use some work. I'm considering adding something to the ending, to make it bittersweet (like Caspian2 recommended). Instead of Ty just transforming completely, basically making him brain dead, he is offered to order a dream that lasts forever. A dream that replicates real life. However, it will always be the summer of 1965, and his physical body will be completely transformed. With no other option, Ty accepts the offer, and he falls asleep for the last time.<br />
Of course, this is just an idea, and I'll probably brainstorm other endings that might work better.</p>
<p>The reason he knows who The Oneiroi Collective are is more simple. Whenever anyone picks up the phone on SCP-1498, someone claiming to be from The Oneiroi Collective will answer the call.<br />
The reason he finds anomalous abilities is slightly more complex. Ty's main flaw as a character is that he's driven by boredom, and nothing else. All his actions at the beginning of the tale are taken without consideration, as he only takes those actions to relieve himself of boredom. So, when he finds the SCP, although he's at first startled, he eventually becomes enthralled and starts to inspect it, eventually using the phone, in which the main plot begins. He gets addicted to using the SCP not only because it's one of its anomalous abilities, but also because it seems to be a way to escape the boredom of his mind. Of course, he gets more than he bargains for.<br />
If you're asking why he thinks that it's the SCP causing the changes to his body, it's more or less a hopeful guess on his part. He makes the connection between the phone related changes to the phone related sheep and assumes that it's the SCP causing the issues (which, he is correct). As usual, this detail could be ironed out more.</p>
<p>Again, thanks for responding. I think I'm going to start writing the draft. When that's finished and edited, I'll submit it to the draft critique forum and probably PM you.</p>
<p>Have a great day, and I hope you had a merry Christmas!</p>
<p>Sincerely, Gravy.</p>

